%!PS-Adobe-3.0 Resource-ProcSet
%%Title: ColorRendering
%%Creator: stet
%%EndComments

% The ColorRendering ProcSet that findcolorrendering consults (PLRM 3rd ed., section 7.1.3 and the
% findcolorrendering operator). Programs that select a CRD (Illustrator's and CorelDRAW's EPS prologs) copy it,
% replace GetSubstituteCRD and define it again, so findcolorrendering looks it up on every call.

<<
    % - GetPageDeviceName name: the page device's PageDeviceName, or /none.
    /GetPageDeviceName {
        currentpagedevice dup /PageDeviceName known
            { /PageDeviceName get dup null eq { pop /none } if }
            { pop /none }
        ifelse
    } bind
    % - GetHalftoneName name: the current halftone's HalftoneName, or /none.
    /GetHalftoneName {
        currenthalftone dup /HalftoneName known
            { /HalftoneName get }
            { pop /none }
        ifelse
    } bind
    % intent GetSubstituteCRD name: the CRD to use when none is named for this intent, device and halftone.
    /GetSubstituteCRD { pop /DefaultColorRendering } bind
>>
